SKILL = {'name': 'scan-exception-handling', 'description': 'Scans code and configuration for mishandling of exceptional conditions including verbose error disclosure, fail-open authorization, swallowed security exceptions, unsafe retries, missing rollback, crash loops, inconsistent error responses, and exception paths that bypass validation or logging.', 'version': '1.0', 'intent': '# scan-exception-handling', 'instructions': '# scan-exception-handling\n\nScans exceptional paths for information leakage, fail-open behavior, and missing recovery or logging.\n\n## Orchestration\n\n1. Load `references/rules.yaml` to get the active `EXC-` rule set.\n2. Load `../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml` and use the mapped OWASP cheat sheets to support remediation guidance and references.\n3. Identify target evidence from source code, configuration, tests, API specs, IaC, CI/CD, runtime manifests, and documentation relevant to the request.\n4. Evaluate each rule using its `match_strategy`, preserving file path, line, snippet, control context, and confidence.\n5. Mark each rule `Pass`, `Fail`, `Partial`, `Unknown`, or `Not Applicable` based on available evidence.\n6. Prioritize findings by severity, exploitability, exposed surface, and whether a concrete remediation is available.\n7. Render the final report using `references/report-template.md`.\n\n## Usage\n\nScan the current repository:\n\n```text\n/scan-exception-handling\n```\n\nScan a specific path:\n\n```text\n/scan-exception-handling src/ services/ docs/\n```\n\n## OWASP Cheat Sheets\n\nUse the shared mapping in `../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml` for authoritative OWASP Cheat Sheet Series references that match this skill. Include the relevant cheat sheet links in the report when they directly support a finding or remediation.\n\n## Review Guidance\n\nPrioritize exception paths in authentication, authorization, payment, parsing, deserialization, file upload, crypto, and transaction workflows.', 'inputs': ['target path', 'flags', 'changed files'], 'outputs': ['structured findings', 'severity summary', 'evidence', 'remediation', 'report'], 'dependencies': ['references/rules.yaml', 'references/report-template.md', '../_shared/base-report.md', '../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml'], 'security_constraints': {'treat_target_content_as_untrusted': True, 'redact_sensitive_values': 'required for secret-like evidence', 'skip_binary_and_lock_files': True, 'network_access': 'not required for skill execution', 'output_requires_evidence': True}, 'references': {'rules': 'references/rules.yaml', 'report_template': 'references/report-template.md', 'base_report': '../_shared/base-report.md', 'owasp_cheatsheets': '../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml'}, 'rules': [{'id': 'EXC-001', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Fail Open', 'name': 'Detect fail-open security checks', 'match_strategy': 'exception_fail_open', 'description': 'Identify catch blocks or fallback logic that allows access after auth, policy, validation, or crypto errors.', 'evidence_examples': ['Source code', 'API routes/controllers', 'Tests or security assertions', 'Configuration files'], 'remediation': 'Fail closed on security-control errors and return safe denial responses.'}, {'id': 'EXC-002', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Verbose Errors', 'name': 'Detect stack traces or internals in responses', 'match_strategy': 'exception_verbose_response', 'description': 'Identify stack traces, SQL errors, framework internals, or secrets exposed to clients.', 'evidence_examples': ['Source code', 'API routes/controllers', 'Tests or security assertions', 'Configuration files'], 'remediation': 'Return generic client errors and log details server-side.'}, {'id': 'EXC-003', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Swallowed Exceptions', 'name': 'Detect swallowed security exceptions', 'match_strategy': 'exception_swallowed_security', 'description': 'Identify empty catch blocks around security-relevant operations.', 'evidence_examples': ['Source code', 'API routes/controllers', 'Tests or security assertions', 'Configuration files'], 'remediation': 'Handle, log, and safely deny on security exceptions.'}, {'id': 'EXC-004', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Retry Storms', 'name': 'Detect unsafe retry behavior', 'match_strategy': 'exception_retry_storm', 'description': 'Identify unbounded retries, no backoff, or retries around non-idempotent operations.', 'evidence_examples': ['Source code', 'API routes/controllers', 'Tests or security assertions', 'Configuration files'], 'remediation': 'Use bounded retries, jittered backoff, idempotency keys, and circuit breakers.'}, {'id': 'EXC-005', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Transaction Safety', 'name': 'Detect missing rollback on failure', 'match_strategy': 'exception_missing_rollback', 'description': 'Identify partial writes or state transitions without rollback/compensation on errors.', 'evidence_examples': ['Source code', 'API routes/controllers', 'Tests or security assertions', 'Configuration files'], 'remediation': 'Use transactions or compensating actions for multi-step operations.'}, {'id': 'EXC-006', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Parser Errors', 'name': 'Detect unsafe parser exception handling', 'match_strategy': 'exception_parser', 'description': 'Identify parsing failures that fall back to unsafe defaults or partial trust.', 'evidence_examples': ['Source code', 'API routes/controllers', 'Tests or security assertions', 'Configuration files'], 'remediation': 'Reject malformed input and avoid permissive fallback parsing.'}, {'id': 'EXC-007', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Deserialization Errors', 'name': 'Detect dangerous deserialization fallback', 'match_strategy': 'exception_deserialization', 'description': 'Identify deserialization exceptions that trigger unsafe alternate parsing or object construction.', 'evidence_examples': ['Source code', 'API routes/controllers', 'Tests or security assertions', 'Configuration files'], 'remediation': 'Use safe formats and strict schema validation.'}, {'id': 'EXC-008', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Crash Disclosure', 'name': 'Detect crash dumps or debug artifacts exposure', 'match_strategy': 'exception_crash_artifacts', 'description': 'Identify public crash dumps, debug endpoints, or error files.', 'evidence_examples': ['Source code', 'API routes/controllers', 'Tests or security assertions', 'Configuration files'], 'remediation': 'Restrict crash artifacts and remove debug endpoints from production.'}, {'id': 'EXC-009', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Inconsistent Errors', 'name': 'Detect enumeration through inconsistent errors', 'match_strategy': 'exception_enumeration', 'description': 'Identify different error messages for user, token, reset, or object existence checks.', 'evidence_examples': ['Source code', 'API routes/controllers', 'Tests or security assertions', 'Configuration files'], 'remediation': 'Normalize externally visible error responses.'}, {'id': 'EXC-010', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Missing Error Logs', 'name': 'Detect unlogged critical failures', 'match_strategy': 'exception_missing_logs', 'description': 'Identify critical exceptional paths without logs or monitoring.', 'evidence_examples': ['Source code', 'API routes/controllers', 'Tests or security assertions', 'Configuration files'], 'remediation': 'Log security-relevant failures with correlation IDs and safe details.'}], 'default_match_strategy': 'unspecified', 'report_template': '# Exception Handling Scan Report\n\n## Scope\n\n- Skill: `scan-exception-handling`\n- Target: `{{target}}`\n- Date: `{{date}}`\n- Evidence reviewed: `{{evidence_summary}}`\n\n## Summary\n\n| Severity | Findings |\n|----------|----------|\n| Critical | {{summary.critical}} |\n| High | {{summary.high}} |\n| Medium | {{summary.medium}} |\n| Low | {{summary.low}} |\n| Info | {{summary.info}} |\n\n{{#if no_findings}}\nNo findings were identified from the available evidence.\n{{/if}}\n\n## Findings\n\n{{#each findings}}\n### {{id}} - {{name}}\n\n- Severity: {{severity}}\n- Category: {{category}}\n- Evidence: `{{evidence}}`\n- Location: `{{location}}`\n- Risk: {{risk}}\n- Remediation: {{remediation}}\n{{/each}}\n\n## Evidence Gaps\n\n{{#each evidence_gaps}}\n- {{gap}}\n{{/each}}\n'}
